    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0403" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/4–2947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Rangoon</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Packer</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">immediate</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rangoon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-29T08:00:00+06:30">April 29, 1947—8
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Shwe Baw has requested me inform Dept Governor<anchor n="78"
                        xml:id="d324-f1"/> today telegraphed Secretary of State for Burma<anchor
                        n="79" xml:id="d324-f2"/> that Burma desires be represented proposed Far
                    Eastern Commission Tokyo in May on Jap reparations. He said Executive Council
                    disappointed it had had no opportunity present its views before decision reached
                    (Dept Wireless Bulletin April 4<anchor n="80" xml:id="d324-f3"/>) alloting only
                    5% for UK, Burma, Malaya, et cetera, and was inclined blame HMG; it felt Burma’s share of these 3% insufficient
                    and inequitable.</p>
                <p>British group of four members, he said, was due leave London for Tokyo April 21
                    but had no information whether it had actually departed from UK.</p>
                <p>I promised inform Dept.</p>
                <p>In this connection see Rangoon press clippings series No. 3, April 12<anchor
                        n="80" xml:id="d324-f4"/> items <hi rendition="#italic">g</hi> 5 and 6.</p>
                <p>Relay London as 68.<anchor n="81" xml:id="d324-f5"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Packer</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
